          "date": "2026-10-29 04:33:31.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20909 tests: size sanity-ec/12e,12f in client pages",
        "message": "LU-20909 tests: size sanity-ec/12e,12f in client pages\n\nsanity-ec test_12e and test_12f assumed a 4KiB client PAGE_SIZE.\nParity resync aligns its coverage ranges to the client page size,\nso on a 16KiB-page client test_12e would find no parity hole at\n[8k, 16k), since that lies inside page 0 which has data, and\ntest_12f would find parity written up to 16384 instead of 4096:\n\n  test_12e: mirror 2 lseek -l at 0: 8192 != 1048576\n  test_12f: mirror 2 lseek -l at 0: 4096 != 16384\n\nExpress the punch offsets and the expected parity hole and data\nranges in units of PAGE_SIZE.  With 4KiB pages the values are\nunchanged.\n\nFixes: 3f1db078c51b (\"LU-12668 ec: ensure hole ranges for raidset parity\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec clientarch=aarch64 clientdistro=rocky9.8 env=ONLY=\"12e 12f\"\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I89eb735f91c74d1cf491787c27044a11b73ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
